{
  "original_prompt": "You label documents from a corpus about Streets and Mobility. Fill in every field:\n- category: the single 311 service category for this request -- one of Road/Street Issues, Traffic and Street Sign Issues, Street Light, Pedestrian/Bicycle Concerns, Parking.\n- department: the exact city unit that should handle the request -- a short value taken from the document.\n- entities: neighborhoods, streets or intersections named in the text, copied exactly -- a list of strings.",
  "revised_prompt": "You are labeling a Pittsburgh 311 street complaint. Return ONLY a flat JSON object with exactly these three keys: category, department, entities. Do NOT wrap in 'type', 'properties', 'required', or any schema keywords. Do NOT add explanation.\n\nExample of the EXACT format required:\n{\"category\": \"Street Light\", \"department\": \"Allegheny City Electric\", \"entities\": [\"Forbes Ave\", \"Squirrel Hill\"]}\n\nRules:\n- category MUST be exactly one of: Road/Street Issues, Traffic and Street Sign Issues, Street Light, Pedestrian/Bicycle Concerns, Parking\n- department MUST be one of: DPW - Street Maintenance, DOMI - Asphalt, DOMI - Traffic, DOMI - Permits, DOMI - Construction, DOMI - Streets, Pittsburgh Water and Sewer Authority, Allegheny City Electric, DPW - Park Maintenance, Police - AVU, Police - Zones 1-6, Parking Authority, Permits, Licenses and Inspections, 311\n- Routing: pothole/snow/sinkhole/drainage/overgrowth -> DPW - Street Maintenance; repaving -> DOMI - Asphalt; sign repair or signal repair -> DOMI - Traffic; streetlight REPAIR -> Allegheny City Electric; new streetlight -> DOMI - Permits; generic 'Sign' complaint -> Permits, Licenses and Inspections; sidewalks/bike infra -> DOMI - Permits or Permits, Licenses and Inspections; illegal parking -> Police - Zones 1-6; abandoned vehicle -> Police - AVU; meters/permits -> Parking Authority\n- entities: list neighborhoods and streets exactly as written in the text; empty list if none\n\nReturn the flat JSON object now, nothing else.",
